      "nclexEssential": true,
      "quickAnswer": "ACHES is a warning-sign cue, not a diagnosis. New severe symptoms require assessment for thromboembolism, stroke, cardiac disease, liver or gallbladder disease, pregnancy complications, or another cause.",
